  "verbalization": "Hirsutene appears to interact with LoVo cells, which are targeted by multiple compounds, including Hirsutene, (+)-(6S)-hydroxymenthol, and (2S)-2,3-Bis((1-oxohexadecyl)oxy)propyl 6-deoxy-6-sulfo-alpha-D-glucopyranoside. All these compounds are linked to the CD70 antigen, suggesting a potential mechanism where Hirsutene may influence the expression or activity of CD70 antigen through interaction with LoVo cells. The evidence implies that Hirsutene could act as a modulator of CD70 antigen expression, possibly by targeting LoVo cells, which in turn may upregulate or downregulate CD70 antigen. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of multiple compounds targeting LoVo cells and their subsequent effect on CD70 antigen indicates a possible pathway involving cell surface interactions or signaling pathways, though further investigation is needed to clarify the precise mechanism.",
